xnu 0416: read the AW88261 IDs over SE15 I2C (mondrianaudioprobe=1)

The audio donor cannot produce sound yet, but the first hardware question is
whether both speaker amplifiers answer on their board buses. This opt-in
worker maps only the four TLMM pages, pulses the active-low shutdown lines,
bit-bangs SDA/SCL and reads register 0x00 at 0x34/0x35. It writes no amp
data register, votes no rail, clocks no QUP and starts no ADSP or PCM path.

The register number, expected 0x2113 and big-endian wire format are protocol
facts from mainline aw88261.c/.h (GPL-2.0-only); no Linux or vendor code
is copied. Board constants come from dtb/mondrian-live.dtb.

